Z||000000||Monkeyman||09-15-2001||09:59 PM||||My Grant steering wheel spokes are anodized aluminum (black if it matters).  I have some minor scratches in them and was wondering what to do.  I'm not about to buy another wheel for something this minor, but I'd like to fix it somehow.  I don't think that black paint will look very good.  Any suggestions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||09-15-2001||10:15 PM||||Try a sharpie marker. Might be temporary, but cheap!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-15-2001||10:21 PM||||I'll give it a shot.  I don't mind temporary as long as it works and looks good.  Thanx.<P>------------------<BR>In memory of those that died on 11 Sept 2001.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1367.gif">  <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||1
Z||000003||California Kid||09-15-2001||10:38 PM||||Satin Black shouldn't look too bad, will give a somewhat metal appearance.<P>You might try spraying a sample panel in gloss black, letting it dry real good, then hitting it with steel wool (straight wipe across or with spoke). Experiment !<P>While you could probably find someone to clean the surface up and re-anodize, it probably cost more than a new wheel.||||reg||1
